      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1900-12-07_WidnesExaminer_art0098" n="art0098">
        <head>Warrington v. Chirk,</head>
        <p>Warrington v. Chirk,</p>
        <p>The visit of Chirk to Warrington was attended by a fair gate. Plkying with commendable dash, the War- ringtonians astonished thsmselves and their supporters by completely penning the Welshmen. Morris, in goal, was repeatedly called upon to handle,and the game was twenty minutes old when a splendid effort by Riley culminated in Copeland opening the scoring account. Another brilliant effort by Riley placed Warrington further ahead, and at the interval the locals enjoyed a two goals lead. On turning round the champions soon made their presence felt, and several beautiful concerted movements caused Aspirsall trouble. Chirk would not be denied, and I Roberts gaining two goals in quick suc- cession, the superior stamina of the visitors told its tale, and another passing movement saw Wynn gain another goal,Chirk winning an interesting game by three goals to two. The visitors owe their victory to the all-round ex- cellence of their combination, an i Warrington have learned an object le.son in the passing art. Oswestry Win at Newton-le-Willows.</p>
        <p>Oswestry brought a strong side, including the old Everton player, Parry to Newton-le-Willows, and easily captured a couple of points. Oswestry asserted their superiority, the first goal being registered before the came was five minutes old, trom the foot of Gooderidge The ball had not been long restarted when the burly Parry planted the leather past Lowe again. Fortunately the Newton defence was not penetrated again up to half time, when the score was =banged. A desperate</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1900-12-07_WidnesExaminer_art0099" n="art0099">
