        <p>ST. ANNE'S NEW SCHOOLS.—URGENT APPEAL. The following extracts from Her Majesty's Inspectors of Schools show the great need and extreme urgency for new Schools.</p>
        <p>"If the increased accommodation for Infants which is much needed in this part of Warrington 13 not supplied by the extension of these buildings as proposed by the Managers last year. a new school will be required in the Immediate neighbourhood." " Her Majesty's Inspector reports that the Class-room of the Jurkior Mixed Department is habitually used for a larger number of Scholars than that for which it is passed by this Board." " In view of the continued overcrowding of the Senior Mixed Departrnent.and the need for increased Infant RC- commociation the Board of Education trust that they will receive from your Managers, an early intimation, that the plans approved on the 17th April, 1899 will be carried out without delay." SUBSCRIPTIONS may be sent to.—St. Anne's New School Fund, Parr's Bank, or to the following Managers :—The Rey J. DAVIES, Chairman, Folly-lane ; ED ,ARD ROSE, Esq., Treasurer, The Blue Coat School; WILLIAM RICHARDSON. Correspondent, holly Bank, Walton, Warrington ; JOHN BAIRD, Froghall-lane.</p>
