        <p>attempt was made by 1 c vier-; IF to pet cc lc terms'in the second half, and Worrall scored a capital goal for them, but the visitors added two more, and just before the close Kenny added a second goal for Newton, who lost a good game by four goals to two. Undoubtedly the visitors deserved their victory, and played better all-round football than Newton. HOCKEY. Latchford'A" v. Eccles. These teams met at Latchford, on Saturday, and des- pite the inclement state of the weather and treacherous ground a very enjoyable game was witnessed. As this is the first season for both teams the best of hockey was not always displayed, both sides missing some easy chances. The hcmesters had rather the best of the game throughout, the visiting custodian saving some good shots, thus neutralizing their efforts. The Brothers Spensley scored the only two goals of the match. Final score Latchford, two ; Eccles. nil. Stockton Heath v. Huyton. Stockton Heath were at home to Huyton,who defeated them by three goals to two. The game throughout was of an exceptionally even and Interesting nature. The Huyton forwards were, however, a little smarter on the ball than the horaesters, and this gained them the ver- dict.</p>
