        <p>" The Land 0' Cakes" was the next toast and it was entrusted to Mr. May, Mr. Ewart responding. The Chairman submitted the toast of " the town and trade of Warrington" and Councillor Tinnon responded on .behalf of the town and Mr Niel on behalf of the trade, "The Lassies" was proposed by Mr Fletcher and responded to by Mr Robson, Other toasts included " Our Visitors," and" The Host and Hostess." Musical items were agreeably interspersed, The Orpheus Male Voice Choir contributed" Annie Laurie "and "Bonnie Doon." Solos were also sung by Councillor For- shaw, Mr Hunter, Mr Davenport and Mr White- house. the accompaniments being supplied by Mr Frank Booth. A pleasant gathering concluded with the P ing in g of" Auld Lang Syns " and the National Anthem.</p>
